# Model/data artifacts.
#
# backend/artifacts/ IS committed (via LFS). The whole directory used to be
# ignored, which meant the deployed Space had no artifacts at all: the model
# registry raised FileNotFoundError and /predict silently degraded to
# _fallback_predict, whose crop recommender only sees N/P/K/pH/temp/humidity/
# rainfall. With no state or district feature, every district returned the
# identical crop and confidence, and district intelligence was always empty.
#
# Only the genuinely regenerable/unused parts stay ignored:
#   */advisor/     - per-state yield models (236 MB) no runtime path reads
#   fallback_events.jsonl, sync_state.json - runtime logs written in-place
backend/artifacts/*/advisor/
backend/artifacts/edge/fallback_events.jsonl
backend/artifacts/**/sync_state.json
trained_artifacts_fast/

# Local user files
*.crdownload

# Retrieval caches: AGRIS Open Data Set subsets and per-query enrichment
# results. Regenerated on demand; the ODS subsets alone are ~150 MB.
graph_rag/cache/
.cache/
TerraMind_Datasets/

# Debug residue. error_full.txt is a traceback dump that leaks absolute
# C:\Users\... paths; the python_path*.txt files are dumps of the local PATH
# and interpreter locations. Nothing here describes the project.
error_full.txt
python_path_check.txt
python_paths.txt
test.txt

# Local scratch scripts. These are `python <file>.py` smoke tests with
# sys.path.insert hacks, not a pytest suite - they stay on disk, out of git.
test_pred.py
test_integration.py
backend/test_orchestrator.py

# Generated evaluation plots, rebuilt wholesale by
# ml/growth_stage_monitor/visualize.py. The directory also shadows the
# sibling evaluation.py module, so keeping it out of git avoids the collision.
ml/growth_stage_monitor/evaluation/

# Federated simulation outputs, rewritten by
# federated/run_simulation.py::save_federated_artifacts on every run.
federated/results/*
!federated/results/.gitkeep
